alues":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested with v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9579) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.55 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI exported an empty Node2D scene to HTML.\nBy default, I observed 20% CPU usage in the browser (Chrome and Firefox) Task Manager, which is extremely high for such a simple project.\nSetting max_fps to 30 or enabling low_processor_mode **increases** CPU usage to 80-100%.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create new project (Select Compatibility as renderer)\n- Add Node2D scene and save it, select it as main scene.\n- Install Export Templates\n- Add Export preset for Web\n- Run in browser (shift + F5)\n- Try enabing max_fps or low_processor_mode and run again\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCreate new project with single empty Node2D scene.","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users